{"name":"Evil Curse","hex":"#884488","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"evil","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Intending to harm; malevolent.","Morally corrupt."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Moral badness; wickedness; malevolence; the forces or behaviors that are the opposite or enemy of good.","Something which impairs the happiness of a being or deprives a being of any good; something which causes suffering of any kind to sentient beings; harm; injury; mischief."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/evil"},{"term":"curse","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A supernatural detriment or hindrance; a bane.","A prayer or imprecation that harm may befall someone."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To place a curse upon (a person or object).","To call upon divine or supernatural power to send injury upon; to imprecate evil upon; to execrate."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/curse"}],"entries":[{"title":"Evil","blocks":[{"text":"Evil, as a concept, is usually defined as profound immorality, and it is related to acts that cause pain and suffering to others."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Demon._A_miniature_from_the_Georgian_manuscript_of_the_12th_century.jpg/330px-Demon._A_miniature_from_the_Georgian_manuscript_of_the_12th_century.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Evil"},{"title":"Curse","blocks":[{"text":"A curse is any expressed wish that some form of adversity or misfortune will befall or attach to one or more persons, a place, or an object. In particular, \"curse\" may refer to such a wish or pronouncement made effective by a supernatural or spiritual power, such as a god or gods, a spirit, or a natural force, or else as a kind of spell by magic or witchcraft; in the latter sense, a curse can also be called a hex or a jinx. In many belief systems, the curse itself is considered to have some causative force in the result. To reverse or eliminate a curse is sometimes called \"removal\" or \"breaking\", as the spell has to be dispelled, and often requires elaborate rituals or prayers."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/A_woman_makes_a_cursing_ritual_ceremony.jpg/330px-A_woman_makes_a_cursing_ritual_ceremony.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Curse"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Ary_Scheffer_-_The_Temptation_of_Christ_%281854%29.jpg/500px-Ary_Scheffer_-_The_Temptation_of_Christ_%281854%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Ary_Scheffer_-_The_Temptation_of_Christ_%281854%29.jpg/1280px-Ary_Scheffer_-_The_Temptation_of_Christ_%281854%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Ary_Scheffer_-_The_Temptation_of_Christ_%281854%29.jpg/500px-Ary_Scheffer_-_The_Temptation_of_Christ_%281854%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The devil, in opposition to the will of God, represents evil and tempts Christ, the personification of the character and will of God. Ary Scheffer, 1854.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAry_Scheffer_-_The_Temptation_of_Christ_(1854).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Extermination_of_Evil_Sendan_Kendatsuba_crop.jpg/500px-Extermination_of_Evil_Sendan_Kendatsuba_crop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Extermination_of_Evil_Sendan_Kendatsuba_crop.jpg/1280px-Extermination_of_Evil_Sendan_Kendatsuba_crop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","